  "description": "BALMOS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H88 Er4 N8 O38,2(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.542-3.894 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.63-111.88°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er4(μ3-OH)4(H2O)2(npd)8]·1.5 toluene. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
